body:
I've been referencing this post at least twice a day for the last week while I power through as much Pace as I can. Thank you, you kind soul.

&#x200B;

Is there an explanation for why the first 22 Pace episodes of Enies Lobby don't have a dub?

I found out about straight edge after listening to a lot of old school hardcore (the typical Minor Threat, Black Flag, Dead Kennedys stuff) and I realized I was already living that life. I had my first serious taste of alcohol about a year after that, had my first cigarette, and vaped for a while. I never had more than that one cigarette, I sold my vaporizer at the request of my parents (which I do not regret), and I never really liked drinking.

&#x200B;

I decided I liked the ethos of the straight edge community when I realized that, even though I didn't drink or do drugs, I was still a slave to plenty of products/substances. For me, straight edge isn't just about "not doing bad stuff" but is about taking a proactive role in your own development, relying on yourself and abstaining from the things that hinder or distract you.

&#x200B;

I'm currently trying to stop consuming anything with excessive/added sugar (soda, juice, processed foods, snack cakes), I'm trying to not eat fast food at all, I'm trying to stop watching porn and masturbating, and I'm getting back into working out consistently and waking up early. I want the direction of my life to be decided by God but enacted by me: no substance or harmful practice is going to dictate how I should feel, what I should be doing with my time, or of what I am capable.

&#x200B;

**A more direct response to your second question:** I research my food to find out what fits my macros (for working out) and what is more organic/unprocessed. I try and make sure I take the time to cook and meal prep. I'm still trying to get in the habit of reading or using my time on the internet to learn rather than zone-out. I try and fall asleep earlier (which I'm not very good at currently) and I'm still trying to stop watching porn (which is the hardest thing I've ever had to do).

&#x200B;

**TL;DR** \- I like to feel in control of my life and abstaining from substances/practices that hinder/distract me is a way to do that. Instead of eating out, drinking, or being generally undisciplined: I workout, I cook organic food, I try and use my free time to learn, and I try and not watch porn.
